		<r3d:repositoryName language="eng">Constrained Local UniversE Simulations</r3d:repositoryName>
				<r3d:additionalName language="eng">CLUES</r3d:additionalName>
				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://www.clues-project.org/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The main goal of the CLUES-project is to provide constrained simulations of the local universe designed to be used as a numerical laboratory of the current paradigm. The simulations will be used for unprecedented analysis of the complex dark matter and gasdynamical processes which govern the formation of galaxies. The predictions of these experiments can be easily compared with the detailed observations of our galactic neighborhood.
Some of the CLUES data is now publicly available via the CosmoSim database (https://www.cosmosim.org/). This includes AHF halo catalogues from the Box 64, WMAP3 resimulations of the Local Group with 40963 particle resolution.</r3d:description>
